raceback (per_workload has only status). Remaining shared, untouched suspects live in conv1_kernel / conv_nhwc_kernel / linear_kernel / run(); addressing math re-verified correct. Strongest remaining hypothesis: the version-fragile pipelined loop construct `tl.range(...)` used in conv2/conv3/linear (the dot-using kernels). conv1 launches first and has NO tl.range, so a tl.range compile failure in conv2 is consistent with an all-workloads RUNTIME_ERROR. Next c004: replace every `tl.range(...)` with canonical Python `range(...)` over constexpr bounds (official Triton matmul tutorial form), keep num_stages conservative.\"}\n{\"candidate_id\": \"c004\", \"candidate\": \"c004\", \"parent\": \"c003\", \"source_sha256\": \"28fc78e63b6545da03a1310a065503eff7f3825a399b5c70a17762a5a8f92c64\", \"phase\": \"feedback\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T20:01:03Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"The uniform RUNTIME_ERROR is a Triton compile error in the dot-using kernels (conv2/conv3/linear). The remaining version-fragile construct is `tl.range(...)` (a pipelined-loop hint). Replacing every `tl.range(0,..,BLOCK_K)` inner k-loop with canonical Python `range(...)` (official matmul tutorial form) and lowering all dot-kernel num_stages to 2 should let it compile.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"conv2/conv3/linear inner k-loops: `tl.range(...)` -> `range(...)`; num_stages 3->2 for all three dot-kernel launches. conv1 and all math/layout/addressing unchanged.\", \"changes_vs_parent\": \"loop construct (tl.range->range) + num_stages 3->2 on the three dot kernels.\", \"validation\": {\"structural_guards\": \"pass\", \"all_workloads_pass\": false, \"per_workload\": [{\"wl\": \"w1\", \"uuid\": \"9415ba43-1612-5a34-a400-0e351edb434e\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w2\", \"uuid\": \"dedae7e8-65de-5163-9c0e-4cf292aef154\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \