cc = tl.dot(a,w,acc)` (tutorial-exact, no out_dtype kwarg); (b) conv1_kernel itself (unchanged since c001) or run()-setup asserts. Next c005: switch all three dots to the accumulate form. If still RUNTIME_ERROR, the dot convention is cleared and the following candidate will target conv1/run() directly (e.g., a diagnostic that isolates whether conv1 alone executes).\"}\n{\"candidate_id\": \"c005\", \"candidate\": \"c005\", \"parent\": \"c004\", \"source_sha256\": \"57b1f16f1e80e2bdca7d2dbb5badd647e23b5f1b699006871a09cac8a36ba08a\", \"phase\": \"feedback\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T21:12:24Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"The uniform RUNTIME_ERROR is a Triton compile error at the tl.dot call convention. All three dot kernels used `acc += tl.dot(a, w, out_dtype=tl.float32)`; the `out_dtype=` kwarg is version-fragile. Switch every call to the tutorial-exact 3-arg accumulate form `acc = tl.dot(a, w, acc)` (fp32 accumulator carried in positionally, no out_dtype kwarg). Semantically identical fp32 accumulation.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"All three `acc += tl.dot(a, w, out_dtype=tl.float32)` (conv2/conv3/linear) -> `acc = tl.dot(a, w, acc)`. No other changes.\", \"changes_vs_parent\": \"tl.dot call convention only (out_dtype kwarg -> 3-arg accumulate form).\", \"validation\": {\"structural_guards\": \"pass\", \"all_workloads_pass\": false, \"per_workload\": [{\"wl\": \"w1\", \"uuid\": \"9415ba43-1612-5a34-a400-0e351edb434e\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w2\", \"uuid\": \"dedae7e8-65de-5163-9c0e-4cf292aef154\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w3\", \"uuid\": \"c8362d74-604f-509b-8b18-86ff78b4316f\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w4\", \"uuid\": \"67119fc1-69aa-53a7-acd5-dae7dbbcbd56\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w5\", \"uuid\": \"10361f03-c94e-514e-bb4a-6799525e65d5\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}]}, \"workloads\": [{\"uuid\": \"9415ba43-1612-5a34-a400-0e351edb434e\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"dedae7e8-65de-5163-9c0e-4cf292aef154\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"c8362d74-604f-509b-8b18-86ff78b4316f\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"67119fc1-69aa-53a7-acd5-dae7dbbcbd56\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"10361f03-c94e-514e-bb4a-6799525e65d5\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}], \"all_correct\": false, \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": null, \"valid\": false, \"decision\": \"rejected\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 5, \"skills_used\": [], \"skill_usage\": \"KernelWiki: not applicable (Ampere sm_80).\", \"static_checks\": [\"grep-verified all three tl.dot calls now use the 3-arg accumulate form; no out_dtype kwarg remains\"], \"notes\": \"REFUTED: tl.dot call convention was not the cause; identical uniform RUNTIME_ERROR persists. FOUR single-surface fixes (erf/libdevice, broadcast rank, loop-pipelining, dot convention) all refuted, and code inspection of addressing/plumbing found nothing further. Zero observability: the evaluator exposes only status (no traceback), so continued blind single-surface edits are low-information. DECISION: switch strategy from 'fix a suspected surface' to 'bisect for observability'. Next c006 = minimal fully-Triton SMOKE TEST: keep the module intact but in run() launch ONLY a trivial memset Triton kernel to fill the output (real kernels defined but not launched, hence not compiled). If c006 returns INCORRECT (not RUNTIME_ERROR) -> module import + run() plumbing + basic Triton launch all work, so the fault is isolated to the conv/linear kernels (proceed to add them back one at a time). If c006 still RUNTIME_ERROR -> the fault is at import/harness/Triton-availability level, independent of the real kernels, which redirects the entire diagnosis. This diagnostic is fully Triton and NOT a compute fallback (it reports INCORRECT honestly; it never fakes a pass).\"}\n{\"candidate_id\": \"c006\", \"candidate\": \"c006\", \"parent\": \"c005\", \"source_sha256\": \"252db7a7cd127ad03c7181f959c7c520a7d73a086ab69543a01bcb3150e87d6b\", \"phase\": \"feedback\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T22:18:55Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"DIAGNOSTIC (fully Triton, not a compute fallback: returns zeros -> honest INCORRECT, never fakes a pass). After 5 candidates all returned 0/5 uniform RUNTIME_ERROR with zero traceback, pivot to bisection. Keep the module intact (all real kernels defined) but launch ONLY a trivial memset Triton kernel to fill the output. If result is INCORRECT (not RUNTIME_ERROR), module import + run() plumbing + basic Triton JIT launch all work and the compile fault is isolated to the conv/linear kernels; if still RUNTIME_ERROR, the fault is at import/harness level.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"run() now launches ONLY memset_zero_kernel (new trivial @triton.jit) to zero-fill out; the four real kernels are still defined but their launches are moved after an early `return out` (defined-but-not-launched, hence not compiled this candidate).\", \"changes_vs_parent\": \"run() launch site: real 4-kernel pipeline replaced by a single memset launch (diagnostic).\", \"validation\": {\"structural_guards\": \"pass\", \"all_workloads_pass\": false, \"per_workload\": [{\"wl\": \"w1\", \"uuid\": \"9415ba43-1612-5a34-a400-0e351edb434e\", \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null, \"max_abs\": 46948528.0}, {\"wl\": \"w2\", \"uuid\": \"dedae7e8-65de-5163-9c0e-4cf292aef154\", \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w3\", \"uuid\": \"c8362d74-604f-509b-8b18-86ff78b4316f\", \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w4\", \"uuid\": \"67119fc1-69aa-53a7-acd5-dae7dbbcbd56\", \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w5\", \"uuid\": \"10361f03-c94e-514e-bb4a-6799525e65d5\", \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}]}, \"workloads\": [{\"uuid\": \"9415ba43-1612-5a34-a400-0e351edb434e\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\"}, {\"uuid\": \"dedae7e8-65de-5163-9c0e-4cf292aef154\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\"}, {\"uuid\": \"c8362d74-604f-509b-8b18-86ff78b4316f\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\"}, {\"uuid\": \"67119fc1-69aa-53a7-acd5-dae7dbbcbd56\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\"}, {\"uuid\": \"10361f03-c94e-514e-bb4a-6799525e65d5\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\"}], \"all_correct\": false, \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": null, \"valid\": false, \"decision\": \"rejected (diagnostic, expected-INCORRECT)\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 6, \"skills_used\": [], \"skill_usage\": \"KernelWiki: not applicable (Ampere sm_80).\", \"static_checks\": [\"memset kernel uses only tl.program_id/tl.arange/tl.store/tl.zeros; out.view(-1) flatten; grid = cdiv(numel,1024)\"], \"notes\": \"BREAKTHROUGH (observability): result flipped from RUNTIME_ERROR to INCORRECT_NUMERICAL. => module import + run() shape/alloc plumbing + a basic Triton JIT compile+launch ALL WORK. Therefore the persistent RUNTIME_ERROR is isolated to one/more of the real kernels {conv1, conv2, conv3, linear}, NOT import/harness. (Side note: ref max_abs ~4.7e7 vs our zeros -> reference outputs are large; irrelevant to compilation.) Next: BINARY-SEARCH the 4-kernel sequence. c007 = launch conv1 + conv2 (write inter1, inter2) then memset the output. INCORRECT => conv1 & conv2 both compile/run (bug in {conv3, linear}); RUNTIME_ERROR => bug in {conv1, conv2} (conv2 is the first tl.dot kernel). This localizes the raiser in ~2 more evals.\"}\n{\"candidate_id\": \"c007\", \"candidate\": \"c007\", \"parent\": \"c006\", \"source_sha256\": \"11c8c7074e1da38ca193fa642ef11420f6a9ac590f24ddf94bb62da0aee9655f\", \"phase\": \"feedback\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T22:49:33Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"DIAGNOSTIC bisection step 2 (fully Triton; honest INCORRECT on zeros, never fakes a pass). c006 proved import/plumbing/JIT work and isolated the compile fault to {conv1,conv2,conv3,linear}. Launch conv1+conv2 for real (write inter1,inter2), then memset output. INCORRECT => conv1&conv2 both run (raiser in {conv3,linear}); RUNTIME_ERROR => raiser in {conv1,conv2} (conv2 is the first tl.dot kernel, prime suspect).\", \"change_from_parent\": \"run() launch set expanded to conv1_kernel + conv_nhwc_kernel(conv2) writing inter1/inter2, then memset_zero_kernel on out; conv3/linear remain defined-but-not-launched after early return.\", \"changes_vs_parent\": \"launch set: memset-only (c006) -> conv1+conv2+memset (c007).\", \"validation\": {\"structural_guards\": \"pass\", \"all_workloads_pass\": false, \"per_workload\": [{\"wl\": \"w1\", \"uuid\": \"9415ba43-1612-5a34-a400-0e351edb434e\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w2\", \"uuid\": \"dedae7e8-65de-5163-9c0e-4cf292aef154\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w3\", \"uuid\": \"c8362d74-604f-509b-8b18-86ff78b4316f\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w4\", \"uuid\": \"67119fc1-69aa-53a7-acd5-dae7dbbcbd56\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w5\", \"uuid\": \"10361f03-c94e-514e-bb4a-6799525e65d5\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}]}, \"workloads\": [{\"uuid\": \"9415ba43-1612-5a34-a400-0e351edb434e\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"dedae7e8-65de-5163-9c0e-4cf292aef154\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"c8362d74-604f-509b-8b18-86ff78b4316f\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"67119fc1-69aa-53a7-acd5-dae7dbbcbd56\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"10361f03-c94e-514e-bb4a-6799525e65d5\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}], \"all_correct\": false, \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": null, \"valid\": false, \"decision\": \"rejected (diagnostic, localizing)\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 7, \"skills_used\": [], \"skill_usage\": \"KernelWiki: not applicable (Ampere sm_80).\", \"static_checks\": [\"conv1+conv2 launched with same args/tiles as prior candidates; memset after; conv3/linear after early return (uncompiled)\"], \"notes\": \"LOCALIZED to {conv1, conv2}: adding conv1+conv2 to the memset-only baseline flipped INCORRECT (c006) back to RUNTIME_ERROR. Since c006 proved the memset path works, the raiser is conv1 and/or conv2. conv1 is a plain FMA kernel (no tl.dot); conv2 (conv_nhwc_kernel) is the FIRST tl.dot implicit-GEMM. Prime suspect = conv2's tl.dot: operands a=[BLOCK_M,BLOCK_K]=[64,64] bf16 and w loaded as [BLOCK_K,BLOCK_N]=[64,64] bf16 -- shapes are dot-legal (>=16, multiples of 16), so suspicion falls on (a) the strided w load expression `w_ptr + offs_n[None,:]*(CIN*KSZ*KSZ) + kk[:,None]*(KSZ*KSZ) + tap` producing a non-canonical layout Triton's dot dislikes, or (b) conv1's FMA/store. Next c008: bisect conv1 vs conv2 -> launch conv1 ONLY (+ memset out). INCORRECT => conv1 is fine, raiser = conv2 (fix its tl.dot/weight-load); RUNTIME_ERROR => raiser = conv1 (a plain FMA kernel, easy to rewrite).\"}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":4,"oldLines":4,"newStart":4,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"candidate_id\": \"c004\", \"candidate\": \"c004\", \"parent\": \"c003\", \"source_sha256\": \"28fc78e63b6545da03a1310a065503eff7f3825a399b5c70a17762a5a8f92c64\", \"phase\": \"feedback\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T20:01:03Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"The uniform RUNTIME_ERROR is a Triton compile error in the dot-using kernels (conv2/conv3/linear). The remaining version-fragile construct is `tl.range(...)` (a pipelined-loop hint). Replacing every `tl.range(0,..,BLOCK_K)` inner k-loop with canonical Python `range(...)` (official matmul tutorial form) and lowering all dot-kernel num_stages to 2 should let it compile.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"conv2/conv3/linear inner k-loops: `tl.range(...)` -> `range(...)`; num_stages 3->2 for all three dot-kernel launches. conv1 and all math/layout/addressing unchanged.\", \"changes_vs_parent\": \"loop construct (tl.range->range) + num_stages 3->2 on the three dot kernels.\", \"validation\": {\"structural_guards\": \"pass\", \"all_workloads_pass\": false, \"per_workload\": [{\"wl\": \"w1\", \"uuid\": \"9415ba43-1612-5a34-a400-0e351edb434e\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w2\", \"uuid\": \"dedae7e8-65de-5163-9c0e-4cf292aef154\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pa